  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest result so far is RNA-only multi-profile with scVI n200 + transformer aggregation (config_006, acc=0.653), showing that multi-profile representation is the dominant design lever (~13pt gain over single-profile). Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23), and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) is nearly irrelevant. The critical remaining uncertainty is whether fusing the image modality into the already-strong RNA multi-profile pipeline adds any value. This experiment (config_038) tests exactly that: it pairs the best proven RNA setup (scVI n200, multiprofile, transformer) with the slightly stronger image encoder (ViT-L) and a simple concat fusion, changing only the model setting from rna_only to multimodal. This is the highest-information next step because it directly answers whether multimodal fusion is worth the added complexity, and the result will gate whether further multimodal experiments (fusion type, image encoder, aggregation) are warranted under the limited budget."
}

